course: dictionary
lesson: 9551
title: Storage: keeping things until they are needed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Storage means keeping things in a place until you need them. «Families need storage for toys, food and clothes.» The list tells you what storage is for: each thing is kept somewhere safe so it is ready later. A cupboard, a box or a shed can all be storage.
explain: Storage also keeps food safe. «Cold storage» means keeping food cold, such as milk and meat in a fridge, so it stays fresh. Try the swap check: "keeping things until needed" fits the fridge, so your meaning is right.
explain: In computers, storage is the space for saving files and photos. «When a battery runs out, everything stops, and anything not saved to storage is lost.» Saving puts your work into storage, which keeps it even when the power goes off.
explain: «Free space is total storage minus what is used.» Here storage means the total room a device has for saving things. If a device has 64 GB and 30 GB is used, the free space is 34 GB.
fact: Storage is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say «more storage», not «more storages».
fact: Storage means keeping things until they are needed, or the space where they are kept.
fact: «Storage space» and «storage box» are phrases that show where things are kept.
fact: In computing, storage is measured in megabytes (MB) and gigabytes (GB).
fact: «Working memory» (RAM) forgets everything when the power goes off, but storage keeps your saved work.
exercise: «Families need storage for toys, food and clothes.» What does storage mean here? | *A place where things are kept until they are needed | A sudden loud noise | A kind of food | A game played with toys
exercise: Mum says, «We need more storage in the kitchen.» What would the storage most likely be? | A kind of soup | A person who cooks | A type of shoe | *Cupboards and boxes for keeping things
exercise: «Anything not saved to storage is lost.» In a computer, what is storage? | The part that makes sound | The mouse you click with | The screen you look at | *The space for saving files and photos
test: «Cold storage» keeps milk and meat fresh in a fridge. What does cold storage mean? | Keeping things hot in an oven | Cooking food quickly | *Keeping things cold until they are needed | Throwing food away
test: How is computer storage measured? | In metres | In litres | *In gigabytes | In kilograms
exam: «Free space is total storage minus what is used.» A device has 64 GB of storage and 30 GB is used. How much free space is left? | *34 GB | 30 GB | 64 GB | 94 GB
